{"body":[{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28168_4029.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"p","x":"LAS VEGAS, USA (AVING Special Report on 'CES 2007') -- <Visual News> A Japanese company, Nikko, brought R2D2 of Starwars to the CES 2007. Introduced by Dart Vader, the R2D2 at CES 2007 in fact shows up as an advanced projector featuring built-in DVD player and speaker. So, as it was seen in the movie, it can actually record video message and make presentation."},{"t":"p","x":"It can also project 80-inch image in LCOS while it can be controlled with a remote control which looks like a small space-shuttle-shape appeared in the Star Wars movie. The R2D2 also has various video ports, memory expansion slots and iPod docking system."},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28169_4029.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28170_4029.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28171_4029.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28172_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28173_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28174_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"p","x":"This projector projects up to 80 inch and has video port, memory card slot and iPod docking system. Yeah, so, it is somewhat similar to R2D2 of Starwars with iPod compatibility. Cool huh?"},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28175_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28176_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28177_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28178_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us.aving.net/news/photo/200701/6601_28179_4030.jpg","cap":""},{"t":"img","src":"https://cdn.us